  <h2 class="section-title">🕊️ Girls' biblical baby names</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">

    <div class="name-card"><h2>Sarah</h2><div class="pronounce">SAIR-ah</div><div class="meaning">Princess</div><p>Sarah was the wife of Abraham and the mother of Isaac, revered as the first matriarch of Israel. Her name signifies nobility and has been a beloved choice for millennia.</p><div class="origin-tag">👑 matriarch</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Rebekah</h2><div class="pronounce">reh-BEK-ah</div><div class="meaning">To tie · Bound</div><p>Rebekah was the wife of Isaac and mother of Jacob and Esau. Known for her kindness and determination, her name evokes a sense of binding love and loyalty.</p><div class="origin-tag">💧 wellspring</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Rachel</h2><div class="pronounce">RAY-chel</div><div class="meaning">Ewe · Innocent</div><p>Rachel was the beloved wife of Jacob and mother of Joseph and Benjamin. Her name symbolizes gentleness and is one of the most enduring biblical names.</p><div class="origin-tag">🐑 beloved</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Leah</h2><div class="pronounce">LEE-ah</div><div class="meaning">Weary · Delicate</div><p>Leah was Jacob's first wife and mother of six tribes of Israel. Though her name suggests weariness, she is celebrated for her strength and devotion.</p><div class="origin-tag">🌿 matriarch</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Miriam</h2><div class="pronounce">MEER-ee-am</div><div class="meaning">Beloved · Bitter</div><p>Miriam was the sister of Moses and Aaron, a prophetess who led the Israelites in song after the Red Sea crossing. Her name is both powerful and melodic.</p><div class="origin-tag">🎶 prophetess</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Esther</h2><div class="pronounce">ESS-ter</div><div class="meaning">Star</div><p>Esther was a Jewish queen of Persia who saved her people from destruction. Her story of courage is celebrated at Purim, and her name shines like a star.</p><div class="origin-tag">⭐ queen</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Ruth</h2><div class="pronounce">ROOTH</div><div class="meaning">Compassionate friend</div><p>Ruth was a Moabite widow who chose to stay with her mother-in-law Naomi, becoming the great-grandmother of King David. Her name embodies loyalty and love.</p><div class="origin-tag">🤝 loyal</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Hannah</h2><div class="pronounce">HAN-ah</div><div class="meaning">Grace · Favor</div><p>Hannah was the mother of the prophet Samuel. Her heartfelt prayer for a child is one of the most touching stories in scripture, and her name means grace.</p><div class="origin-tag">🙏 grace</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Abigail</h2><div class="pronounce">AB-ih-gail</div><div class="meaning">Father's joy</div><p>Abigail was a wise and beautiful woman who became the wife of King David. Her name radiates joy and is a popular choice for its warm, friendly sound.</p><div class="origin-tag">😊 joy</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Elizabeth</h2><div class="pronounce">eh-LIZ-ah-beth</div><div class="meaning">God is my oath</div><p>Elizabeth was the mother of John the Baptist and a relative of Mary. Her name is regal and deeply rooted in both Old and New Testaments.</p><div class="origin-tag">✝️ oath</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Mary</h2><div class="pronounce">MAIR-ee</div><div class="meaning">Beloved · Pure</div><p>Mary, the mother of Jesus, is the most revered woman in Christianity. Her name is associated with purity, grace, and unwavering faith.</p><div class="origin-tag">🌹 revered</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Martha</h2><div class="pronounce">MAR-tha</div><div class="meaning">Lady · Mistress</div><p>Martha of Bethany was the sister of Mary and Lazarus, known for her hospitality and service. Her name represents strength and practical devotion.</p><div class="origin-tag">🏠 hospitable</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Rebecca</h2><div class="pronounce">reh-BEK-ah</div><div class="meaning">Captivating</div><p>Rebecca is a variant of Rebekah, the matriarch who showed great courage and kindness at the well. It remains elegant and timeless.</p><div class="origin-tag">💧 kind</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Delilah</h2><div class="pronounce">deh-LY-lah</div><div class="meaning">Delicate · Amorous</div><p>Delilah was the woman who betrayed Samson, yet her name is alluring and mysterious. It has a soft, melodic sound that many find appealing.</p><div class="origin-tag">🌙 alluring</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Naomi</h2><div class="pronounce">nay-OH-mee</div><div class="meaning">Pleasant</div><p>Naomi was Ruth's mother-in-law, whose name means "pleasant." Her story of loss and restoration is a testament to faithfulness and redemption.</p><div class="origin-tag">🌾 pleasant</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Judith</h2><div class="pronounce">JOO-dith</div><div class="meaning">Praise</div><p>Judith was a courageous widow who saved her people by defeating Holofernes. Her name is a hymn of praise and is celebrated for its strength.</p><div class="origin-tag">🗡️ brave</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Eve</h2><div class="pronounce">EEV</div><div class="meaning">Life</div><p>Eve was the first woman, mother of all living. Her name is short, elegant, and carries the profound meaning of life itself.</p><div class="origin-tag">🌱 first woman</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Anna</h2><div class="pronounce">AN-ah</div><div class="meaning">Grace</div><p>Anna was a prophetess in the temple who recognized the infant Jesus as the Messiah. Her name is simple, graceful, and beloved worldwide.</p><div class="origin-tag">✨ grace</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Salome</h2><div class="pronounce">sah-LOH-may</div><div class="meaning">Peace</div><p>Salome was a follower of Jesus and the daughter of Herodias. Her name means peace and has a lyrical, exotic quality.</p><div class="origin-tag">🕊️ peace</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Tabitha</h2><div class="pronounce">TAB-ih-thah</div><div class="meaning">Gazelle</div><p>Tabitha, also called Dorcas, was a woman known for her good works and charity. Her name evokes grace and swiftness.</p><div class="origin-tag">🦌 graceful</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Lydia</h2><div class="pronounce">LID-ee-ah</div><div class="meaning">From Lydia</div><p>Lydia was a seller of purple cloth and the first recorded convert to Christianity in Europe. Her name is elegant and historical.</p><div class="origin-tag">💜 merchant</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Priscilla</h2><div class="pronounce">priss-SILL-ah</div><div class="meaning">Ancient</div><p>Priscilla was a devoted Christian leader and wife of Aquila. Her name is classical and carries a sense of wisdom and tradition.</p><div class="origin-tag">📜 ancient</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Zipporah</h2><div class="pronounce">zih-POR-ah</div><div class="meaning">Bird</div><p>Zipporah was the wife of Moses, known for her courage and quick action. Her name is unique and carries a beautiful, winged quality.</p><div class="origin-tag">🐦 bird</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Dinah</h2><div class="pronounce">DY-nah</div><div class="meaning">Judged · Vindicated</div><p>Dinah was the daughter of Jacob and Leah. Her story is one of tragedy and resilience, and her name means justice.</p><div class="origin-tag">⚖️ justice</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Michal</h2><div class="pronounce">mih-KHAL</div><div class="meaning">Who is like God?</div><p>Michal was the daughter of King Saul and wife of David. Her name is a rhetorical question of praise and is distinctive and strong.</p><div class="origin-tag">❓ question</div></div>

  </div>

