  <h2 class="section-title">🛡️ Boys' biblical baby names</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">

    <div class="name-card"><h2>Noah</h2><div class="pronounce">NOH-ah</div><div class="meaning">Rest · Comfort</div><p>Noah was the righteous man who built the ark and saved his family from the flood. His name signifies rest and has become immensely popular worldwide.</p><div class="origin-tag">🚢 ark-builder</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Abraham</h2><div class="pronounce">AY-brah-ham</div><div class="meaning">Father of many</div><p>Abraham is the patriarch of the Israelites, revered for his unwavering faith. His name means "father of a multitude" and is a cornerstone of biblical history.</p><div class="origin-tag">🌟 patriarch</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Isaac</h2><div class="pronounce">EYE-zak</div><div class="meaning">Laughter</div><p>Isaac was the son of Abraham and Sarah, born to them in their old age. His name means "laughter," reflecting the joy of his miraculous birth.</p><div class="origin-tag">😄 laughter</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Jacob</h2><div class="pronounce">JAY-kub</div><div class="meaning">Supplanter</div><p>Jacob, later renamed Israel, was the father of the twelve tribes. His story is one of struggle and transformation, and his name is both classic and strong.</p><div class="origin-tag">💪 wrestler</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Joseph</h2><div class="pronounce">JOH-sef</div><div class="meaning">He will add</div><p>Joseph was the beloved son of Jacob, sold into slavery but risen to power in Egypt. His name represents forgiveness and divine providence.</p><div class="origin-tag">🌾 provider</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Moses</h2><div class="pronounce">MOH-zez</div><div class="meaning">Drawn from the water</div><p>Moses was the great prophet and lawgiver who led the Israelites out of Egypt. His name is synonymous with deliverance and leadership.</p><div class="origin-tag">🌊 deliverer</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Joshua</h2><div class="pronounce">JOSH-oo-ah</div><div class="meaning">The Lord is salvation</div><p>Joshua was Moses' successor who led the Israelites into the Promised Land. His name is a powerful declaration of faith and courage.</p><div class="origin-tag">⚔️ conqueror</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Samuel</h2><div class="pronounce">SAM-yoo-el</div><div class="meaning">God has heard</div><p>Samuel was the prophet who anointed both Saul and David as kings. His name is a testimony to answered prayer and faithful service.</p><div class="origin-tag">👂 heard</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>David</h2><div class="pronounce">DAY-vid</div><div class="meaning">Beloved</div><p>David was the shepherd boy who became king, known for his bravery and his psalms. His name is beloved across cultures and generations.</p><div class="origin-tag">👑 king</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Solomon</h2><div class="pronounce">SOL-oh-mon</div><div class="meaning">Peace</div><p>Solomon was the wise king of Israel who built the first temple. His name is associated with wisdom, justice, and peace.</p><div class="origin-tag">🕊️ wise</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Daniel</h2><div class="pronounce">DAN-yel</div><div class="meaning">God is my judge</div><p>Daniel was a prophet in Babylon who survived the lion's den through his faith. His name is a bold statement of trust in God.</p><div class="origin-tag">🦁 faithful</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Elijah</h2><div class="pronounce">eh-LY-jah</div><div class="meaning">The Lord is my God</div><p>Elijah was a powerful prophet who called down fire from heaven and was taken up in a whirlwind. His name is fiery and commanding.</p><div class="origin-tag">🔥 prophet</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Elisha</h2><div class="pronounce">eh-LY-shah</div><div class="meaning">God is salvation</div><p>Elisha was Elijah's successor, known for his miracles and healing. His name is a beautiful echo of faith and divine intervention.</p><div class="origin-tag">✨ miracle</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Isaiah</h2><div class="pronounce">eye-ZAY-ah</div><div class="meaning">The Lord is salvation</div><p>Isaiah was a major prophet who foretold the coming of the Messiah. His name is poetic and majestic, used in many languages.</p><div class="origin-tag">📜 prophet</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Jeremiah</h2><div class="pronounce">jer-ah-MY-ah</div><div class="meaning">The Lord exalts</div><p>Jeremiah was the "weeping prophet" who called for repentance. His name is strong and resonant, with a deep sense of purpose.</p><div class="origin-tag">💧 weeping</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Ezekiel</h2><div class="pronounce">eh-ZEE-kee-el</div><div class="meaning">God strengthens</div><p>Ezekiel was a prophet of the Babylonian exile, known for his visions of the valley of dry bones. His name is bold and enduring.</p><div class="origin-tag">🦴 visionary</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Matthew</h2><div class="pronounce">MATH-yoo</div><div class="meaning">Gift of the Lord</div><p>Matthew was the tax collector who became one of Jesus' twelve apostles and authored the first Gospel. His name is a gracious gift.</p><div class="origin-tag">📖 evangelist</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Mark</h2><div class="pronounce">MARK</div><div class="meaning">Warlike · Defender</div><p>Mark was the author of the second Gospel and a companion of Peter and Paul. His name is short, strong, and classic.</p><div class="origin-tag">⚔️ defender</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Luke</h2><div class="pronounce">LOOK</div><div class="meaning">Light-giving</div><p>Luke was the physician and author of the third Gospel and Acts. His name radiates warmth and healing.</p><div class="origin-tag">💡 healer</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>John</h2><div class="pronounce">JON</div><div class="meaning">God is gracious</div><p>John was the beloved disciple and author of the fourth Gospel, as well as John the Baptist. His name is one of the most enduring in history.</p><div class="origin-tag">✝️ beloved</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Peter</h2><div class="pronounce">PEE-ter</div><div class="meaning">Rock</div><p>Peter was the foremost of Jesus' apostles, called the rock upon which the church would be built. His name represents steadfast faith.</p><div class="origin-tag">🪨 rock</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Paul</h2><div class="pronounce">PAWL</div><div class="meaning">Small · Humble</div><p>Paul was the great missionary and author of many New Testament letters. His name reflects humility and powerful transformation.</p><div class="origin-tag">📨 missionary</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Timothy</h2><div class="pronounce">TIM-oh-thee</div><div class="meaning">Honoring God</div><p>Timothy was a young companion of Paul and a leader in the early church. His name is gentle and honorable.</p><div class="origin-tag">🙏 honorable</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Andrew</h2><div class="pronounce">AN-droo</div><div class="meaning">Manly · Courageous</div><p>Andrew was the first apostle called by Jesus and the brother of Peter. His name is strong and widely loved.</p><div class="origin-tag">🦁 courageous</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Philip</h2><div class="pronounce">FIL-ip</div><div class="meaning">Lover of horses</div><p>Philip was one of the twelve apostles and a dedicated follower of Jesus. His name is noble and historically rich.</p><div class="origin-tag">🐎 noble</div></div>
    <div class="name-card"><h2>Stephen</h2><div class="pronounce">STEE-ven</div><div class="meaning">Crown · Garland</div><p>Stephen was the first Christian martyr, known for his faith and forgiveness. His name is a crown of courage.</p><div class="origin-tag">👑 martyr</div></div>

